00:26:45.470 --> 00:26:47.120
So let's talk about what.

00:26:47.120 --> 00:26:48.380
What is Cloud Volume Service?

00:26:48.380 --> 00:26:50.690
So as I mentioned,
it's a fully managed,

00:26:50.690 --> 00:26:52.490
cloud native file
services offering,

00:26:52.490 --> 00:26:55.638
that we've built in
partnership with Google Cloud.

00:26:55.638 --> 00:26:57.930
And when I say it's fully
managed, what does that mean?

00:26:57.930 --> 00:26:59.990
It means that you, as
an application owner

00:26:59.990 --> 00:27:03.710
or as a developer, simply go
into the Google Cloud console,

00:27:03.710 --> 00:27:07.750
or with our beta release using
the APIs, provision an NFS

00:27:07.750 --> 00:27:11.630
endpoint that has capacity and
performance characteristics.

00:27:11.630 --> 00:27:13.190
You don't have to
worry about any

00:27:13.190 --> 00:27:16.220
of the backend
infrastructure details

00:27:16.220 --> 00:27:18.020
to actually deliver
that endpoint.

00:27:18.020 --> 00:27:21.590
So capacity planning, networks,
security-- all of that

00:27:21.590 --> 00:27:24.350
is really managed in the
backend by NetApp and Google.

00:27:24.350 --> 00:27:26.840
You simply, as an application
owner or a developer,

00:27:26.840 --> 00:27:29.390
simply consume the endpoint,
with the performance

00:27:29.390 --> 00:27:32.570
and capacity that you need.

00:27:32.570 --> 00:27:34.700
To show the simplicity
of this, actually we're

00:27:34.700 --> 00:27:36.860
